{"hash":"1492b4acb4822947","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":68.262,"said":"Every evening, soon after sunset, the ghats of Varanasi turn to the river for the Ganga Aarti. Its most famous home is Dashashwamedh Ghat, a little way south along this bank. Legend says Brahma himself performed ten ashwamedha sacrifices there, the horse sacrifices that give the ghat its name. On platforms at the water’s edge, priests in saffron stand in a row facing Maa Ganga, just like those below you. Conches are blown, bells ring, and to the rhythm of the bhajans they raise great brass lamps of many flames, moving them up and down and round in slow, wide circles. It lasts about three quarters of an hour, a little earlier in winter and a little later in summer, and every night hundreds gather to watch, on the steps and in boats on the river. On Tuesdays and at festivals, special aartis are held. Sit with the pilgrims here, look out over the water, and listen: the aarti you hear is sung for her.\n\nDid you know? The aarti begins around 7 PM in summer and 6 PM in winter.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":910},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":926,"end":984}],"words":[[0.098,0.421,0,5],[0.531,0.469,6,13],[1.168,0.312,15,19],[1.492,0.3,20,25],[1.805,0.553,26,32],[2.562,0.12,34,37],[2.694,0.361,38,43],[3.067,0.144,44,46],[3.223,0.553,47,55],[3.788,0.3,56,60],[4.101,0.108,61,63],[4.221,0.072,64,67],[4.305,0.409,68,73],[4.726,0.168,74,77],[4.906,0.084,78,81],[5.002,0.433,82,87],[5.447,0.517,88,93],[6.827,0.228,95,98],[7.067,0.325,99,103],[7.404,0.433,104,110],[7.849,0.3,111,115],[8.161,0.12,116,118],[8.293,0.769,119,132],[9.075,0.409,133,137],[9.7,0.06,139,140],[9.772,0.312,141,147],[10.096,0.204,148,151],[10.312,0.421,152,157],[10.745,0.312,158,163],[11.07,0.18,164,168],[11.262,0.433,169,173],[12.572,0.445,175,181],[13.029,0.264,182,186],[13.305,0.385,187,193],[13.702,0.565,194,201],[14.279,0.613,202,211],[14.904,0.337,212,215],[15.252,0.637,216,226],[15.901,0.841,227